    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "JAPAN\nKiamar\nDONG KINGMAN",
      "Cocktaiko\nSherry\nDubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini\nVermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum\nPremium Beer\nMenus\nAperitivo\nApéritif\nFilete de Carne \"Maître d'Hôtel\"\nGrilled beef tenderloin steak with herb butter\nPollo Ranchera\nA chicken saute with a spritely sauce\nFilete de Corvina, Salsa Bercy\nSauteed Fillet of Corvina, served in a sauce of white wine and shallots\nPapas a la Casa\nPotatoes Maison\nLegumbres en Mantequilla\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\nEnsalada Mixta\nTossed Garden Salad\nPostre\nDessert\nCafé\nCoffee\nCafé Descafeinado\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nTé\nTea",
      "Café\nCoffee\nPapas a la Casa\nPotatoes Maison\nLegumbres en Mantequilla\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\nEnsalada Mixta\nTossed Garden Salad\nPostre\nDessert\nCafé Descafeinado\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nTé\nTea\nDrambuie\nSelected Red and White Wines\nChampagne Brut\nAmaretto di Saronno Bénédictine\nCrème de Menthe Cognac VSOP\nCointreau\n378 K490S",
      "JAPAN\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world sketching and painting\nthe beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace more than forty\npermanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad.\nJAPAN is a land of contrasts. It can display the most neon-lit, skyscrapered and expressway-lined\nface vet finds its inspiration in the quiet beauty of the graceful Tori Gate and Mt. Fuji, pictured here\nThe Japanese can run their trains at lightening speed, yet spend hours on a small conversational\ncourtesy. Here vou will find araceful perfection and formality contrasted with vigorous commerce\nAmong the many stylish hotels in the capital city of Tokyo is the Keio Plaza Inter-Continental.\nPan Am serves Tokyo on its Round-The-World flights and nonstop daily from New York, San Francisco.\nLos Angeles, Honolulu, and Hong Kong. Osaka is served nonstop from Honolulu.\nSPAN AM.\n2001.080. 258"
    ],
